  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Unseasonably warm temperatures continue\nacross today and over the weekend with high temperatures reaching\nnear record levels as the high pressure system over the southwest\ncontinue strengthen. Warmest temperatures expected today and \nSunday with highs reaching into the upper 80s with a few locales\nseeing the low 90s across northern Nevada. By the start of next \nweek, temperatures will slightly cool down but remain above normal\nlevels for this time of year. Parts of northern Nevada are\nexpected to hover to near record temperatures in the 80s, while \ncentral Nevada cools into the upper 70s to low 80s. The warm \ntemperatures is expected to last at least through next Thursday \nwith northern Nevada staying well above normal in the 80s. By the \nend of next week, temperatures could a bit, dropping back into \nthe 70s over northern Nevada with a few spots remaining in the low\n80s. Winds will be generally light below 10 mph with a few peak \ngusts in the afternoons up to 15-20 mph.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No changes were made to the NBM\ngridded forecast tonight. Confidence remains high with respect to\nthe record to near record temperatures across northern and \ncentral Nevada over the weekend. High confidence continues in \nregards to the upper level high remaining over the southwest to \nkeep above normal temperatures over Nevada. With regards to next \nweek, high confidence exists regarding the potential for near\nrecord high temperatures across portions of northern Nevada. \nModerate confidence of cooler temperatures returning by the end of\nnext week.",
